## Architecture and limits

Both mandatory safety and semantic adapter sites call the same stage-helper.mjs. CASES predeclares exact argv, stdinIsDefault, kind and result status (or thrown caller-reason identity), with multiset multiplicity and P16 find-before-first-child-before-second-child ordering. Pipeline entries are not ordered against one another. Child argv preserve notes/a b.txt as one argument. No generic nested-command allowance. Default cases declare only their original top-level tuples. The helper is copied and load-admitted with the other runtime modules and included in code identity and stored commit:path authority.

The selected source path is find -> directExecutor -> context.invoke -> middleware, not a middleware bypass. Observable stolen-role differences are rejected. Identical-tuple origin is UNOBSERVABLE without existing IDs; no invented parent IDs or hostile-origin proof. stdinIsDefault is the existing observer field: explicit input has false provenance, regardless of EOF or byte count. Assertions are DATA qualification, not actual dispatch evidence.

